# Stage 18 — the native shell.
#
# The android/ project is GENERATED: `npx cap add android` writes it and
# `npx cap sync` refreshes it from dist/ on every build. Committing it means
# committing a second copy of the app plus a Gradle wrapper, and every
# regenerate lands as a thousand-line diff nobody reads. The config that
# actually decides the shell — capacitor.config.ts — is committed instead,
# so the project can be rebuilt from scratch by anyone with the toolchain.
#
# The one thing that must NEVER be regenerated is the signing keystore: lose
# it and the app can never be updated on a store listing again. It is
# ignored here so it cannot be committed by accident, and stage 19 owns
# backing it up somewhere permanent.
/android/
# `native/android/` is NOT generated: the two Java files the shell needs and
# `cap add android` cannot know about — MainActivity registering the back
# plugin, and the plugin (stage 18b). `npm run apk` copies them in after
# `cap sync`. Hence the leading slash above: only the root project is ignored.
*.keystore
*.jks
key.properties

# The staged APK, copied where a person can find it.
Playball-*.apk

# The signed bundle the store takes lands in the root like the APK does.
*.aab
